WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:05.779
<v Hadi>Teacher, I just saw a shell walk across a ripple in the sand!

00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:12.498
<v Nuri>Let’s watch from here. What can you see sticking out from under the shell?

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:21.897
<v Hadi>Several legs and claws! It’s a hermit crab doing the walking.

00:00:22.447 --> 00:00:29.576
<v Nuri>Yes. The crab’s abdomen is soft. An empty snail shell helps protect it.

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:35.575
<v Nuri>Here is a real Caribbean land hermit crab. Look for the parts outside its shell.

00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:46.574
<v Hadi>When that shell gets tight, will it grow with the crab, or will the crab have to move?

00:00:47.124 --> 00:00:56.013
<v Nuri>Two ideas to test. Remember where each shell is. The crab carries the small one. The bigger one ahead is empty.

00:00:59.163 --> 00:01:08.612
<v Hadi>I’ll watch the little one. If the crab changes homes, that shell should stay behind when it walks away.

00:01:09.162 --> 00:01:15.491
<v Nuri>Watch it back its abdomen into the bigger shell. Now follow the shell that moves.

00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:27.850
<v Hadi>The big shell is moving with the crab. The little one is still on the sand. I can see both at once!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:36.489
<v Nuri>That’s our evidence. The first shell hasn’t grown with the crab. This crab has moved into one with enough room.

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:47.968
<v Nuri>Now let’s visit another coastline in Australia. A white bird is flying over the water. Watch its wings.

00:01:48.518 --> 00:01:55.647
<v Nuri>Here is a real silver gull. Its wings are grey and its legs are red. Can you spot both colours?

00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:07.126
<v Hadi>I’ll draw the shells in my notebook. If I take an empty one home, another crab might need it.

00:02:07.676 --> 00:02:15.125
<v Nuri>That’s a good idea. We can watch and leave the shells where they are. Let’s thank Allah for creating these animals.
